# Trivy ignore list — documented false positives.
#
# Every entry must have a justification. Re-check this list when a new
# Dockerfile or new base image is added to the repository.

# DS-0002 "Container running as root".
#
# back_office/Dockerfile.web and kds/Dockerfile.web use
# nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27-alpine, which runs as UID 101 and
# listens on port 8080. Trivy only checks for a literal `USER`
# instruction in the Dockerfile and does not inspect the base image's
# default user, so it flags these as root even though they are not.
#
# customer_mobile/Dockerfile.web was migrated to nginx-unprivileged on
# 2026-09-25, so the rule no longer matches it either.
DS-0002

# LGPL-3.0-or-later findings for @img/sharp-* are license
# classification, not vulnerabilities. Documented in
# THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md and ADR-016. Trivy's `license` scanner
# classifies them as `restricted`; the project has already reviewed
# the dynamic-linking position and published the required notice.
